    {
      "@id": "x:doc",
      "@type": "Container"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n0",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "The neural mechanisms underlying guilt evoked during such situations of social responsibility are still unknown.",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n1",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "we aimed to assess whether responsibility for these rewards",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n2",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "To better assess whether people’s risk preferences varied between the Solo and the Social condition",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n3",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "happiness decreases following low outcomes for the partner were larger when the participant rather than their partner had made the choice",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n4",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "This guilt effect was associated with BOLD signal increase in the left anterior insula.",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n5",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "suggesting that this part of prefrontal cortex is sensitive to guilt-related information during social choices",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n6",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "the partner’s reward prediction errors (social_pRPE and partner_pRPE) contributed to explaining changes in participants’ momentary happiness",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n7",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "A model-based analysis revealed a left superior temporal sulcus cluster that tracked partner reward prediction errors that followed participant choices.",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n8",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "we do not have strong evidence of differences in risk preferences across conditions",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n9",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "We thus believe that our participants did experience guilt when their choices led to low outcomes for their partner.",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n10",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "being assigned the role of the decider in a social setting may make people slightly unhappy",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n11",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "suggesting people associate a psychological cost with assuming responsibility for others’ outcomes",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n12",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Several brain regions have been associated with the feeling of guilt: the anterior insula (aIns)",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n13",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Deciding for both self and partner rather than just for oneself evoked increased activations in precuneus, left TPJ, and dmPFC",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n14",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "found such responses in the bilateral ventral striatum",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n15",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "demonstrates that participants were not emotionally detached from the consequences of their actions on their partner",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n16",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "participants’ probability of choosing the risky option (lottery) increased with the difference between the expected value of the lottery and the value of the safe option",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n17",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Participants’ reward prediction errors (sRPE) influenced happiness more than partner’s reward prediction errors",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n18",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "suggesting that the information processed in the STS is relayed to the IFG during social decisions",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n19",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "This icebreaker game led to an agreeable social atmosphere and positive, non-competitive, sympathetic attitude between the participants and the partner.",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n20",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "we cannot exclude the possibility that they have instead or in addition felt empathy for their partner",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n21",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Study 1: Figure 2A, t(4796) = 9.26, p < 3.1e–20, β = 0.074",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n22",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Study 2: Figure 2D, t(3829) = 10.62, p < 5.3e–26, β = 0.093",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n23",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Participants chose the lottery more often in the Solo condition than in the Social condition in Study 1",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n24",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "this difference was not found in Study 2 (t(3829) = 0.23, p = 0.82, β = 0.015",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n25",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Study 1: Figure 2B, t(39) = 1.53, p = 0.134, Cohen’s d = 0.24, BF10 = 0.49",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n26",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Study 2: Figure 2E, t(43) = –0.21, p = 0.84, d = –0.03, BF10 = 0.17",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n27",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "participants were slightly more risk averse in the Social than in the Solo condition in Study 1 (Figure 2C, t(39) = 2.27, p = 0.03, d = 0.36, BF10 = 1.69)",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n28",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "(Figure 2F, t(43) = 1.40, p = 0.17, d = 0.21, BF10 = 0.41)",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n29",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "partner reward, Study 1: F(1,2426) = 128.6, p < 0.001, R2 = 0.05",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n30",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "partner reward, Study 2: F(1,1735) = 111.8, p < 0.001, R2 = 0.06",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n31",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Study 1: all LR ≥47.36, p < 0.0001",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n32",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Study 2: all LR ≥77.83, p < 0.0001",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n33",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "weights for social_pRPE were greater than 0: Responsibility model: Study 1: Z = 2.85, p = 0.004",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n34",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Study 2: Z = 3.26, p = 0.001",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n35",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "weights for sRPE were higher than for social_pRPE or partner_pRPE (Study 1: all Z > 6.0, p < 0.001",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n36",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Study 2: all Z > 3.7, p < 0.003",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n37",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "The results show that the estimated parameters could be reliably recovered from noisy synthetic data.",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n38",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Study 1: t(3600) = –3.92, p < 0.0001, β = –0.14",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n39",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Study 2: t(2870) = –6.07, p < 0.0001, β = –0.24",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n40",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Study 1: t(1180) = 3.52, p = 0.0004, β = 0.37, 95% CI = [0.16 0.58]",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n41",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Study 2: t(937) = 2.85, p = 0.0045, β = 0.33, 95% CI = [0.10 0.56]",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n42",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Study 1: t(39) = –3.58, p < 0.001, d = 0.56, BF10 = 32",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n43",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Study 2: t(43) = –2.68, p = 0.01, d = 0.4, BF10 = 3.8",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n44",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Responsibility for choices did not influence happiness following positive lottery outcomes for the partner (both studies, all |t| < 1.3, p > 0.2, BF10 < 0.2).",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n45",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "found such responses in the bilateral ventral striatum (Cohen’s d = 0.72 and 0.85 in the left and right clusters, respectively",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n46",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "in the precuneus (d = 0.79), the left temporo-parietal junction (TPJ; d = 0.59) and the medial prefrontal cortex (mPFC; d = 0.54)",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n47",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Only the precuneus and TPJ showed positive differences in both comparisons (Figure 4C)",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n48",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "and indeed, the insulae showed the sought-after effect",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n49",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "We found a weak response in a small cluster within the left anterior insula (peak T = 3.95, d = 0.59, 22 voxels, peak intensity at [–28 24 –4]",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n50",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "left: pFWE = 0.002, T = 5.63, d = 0.75, Z = 5.41, 110 voxels, peak at MNI [–14 8 –8]",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n51",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "We found this effect in one cluster within the left STS (pFWE = 0.022, T = 4.70, d = 0.53, Z = 4.57, 100 voxels",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n52",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "The first analysis revealed a cluster in the right IFG whose connectivity to the insula (the seed region) was highest when participants made Risky choices for themselves and Safe choices for both players",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n53",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "connectivity was highest when participants made Safe choices for themselves and Risky choices for both players (puncorrected = 0.001, T = 4.44, Z = 4.30, 35 voxels",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n54",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "overall these values were positive (mean = 5.22; median = 6.97; sign test: p = 0.017; Cliff’s Delta = 0.4 = medium effect size",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n55",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "participants’ average ratings of their partners in terms of sympathy, cooperativity, honesty, openness and sociability were all above 8 on a scale of 1–10",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n56",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "These errors evoked activations in the left aIns and dlPFC in the participants (Koban et al., 2013).",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n57",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "activations in anterior middle cingulate cortex and aIns were higher when the pain followed errors made only by the participant rather than by both players",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n58",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "A multivariate reanalysis of these two datasets revealed a neural signature for guilt (Yu et al., 2020)",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n59",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "most participants displayed responsibility aversion, and this effect could not be explained by guilt",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n60",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Forty healthy participants (14 male, mean age 26.1, range 22–31) participated in Study 1 (behaviour only study)",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n61",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "44 healthy participants (19 male, mean (SD) age = 30.6 (6.5), range 23–50) participated in Study 2 (fMRI study)",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n62",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "In another study, partners received painful stimuli when participants made errors during a difficult perception task.",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n63",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "In a variation of this task, participants could decide to bear a proportion of their partner’s pain (Yu et al., 2014).",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n64",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "A recent study by Yu and colleagues re-analysed the results of two previous neuroimaging studies of guilt",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n65",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "participants could delegate their choice between a risky and a safe option to a group or decide themselves",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n66",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "performed three sessions of a task in which they decided on each trial between a safe and a risky monetary option",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n67",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "participants played an ice breaker game with their experiment partner, in which both participant and partner took turns in drawing one half of a simple picture",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n68",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Every two trials, one ISI after the outcome of the previous trial, participants were asked ‘How happy are you right now?’.",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n69",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "we modelled choices with a mixed-effects logistic regression with subject-specific random intercepts",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n70",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "The risk premium for each condition was defined as the EVdiff value corresponding to 50% risky choices",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n71",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "we estimated ⍴ by fitting a probit regression with a cumulative Gaussian link function Φ to choices",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n72",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "we modelled the variations in momentary well-being (happiness ratings) using computational models",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n73",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "added 1SD of noise to the happiness data, fitted the model to these synthetic data, and repeated this procedure 10 times",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n74",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "we regressed Z-scored momentary happiness ratings reported after these outcomes on dummy variables",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n75",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Imaging data were collected on a 3T Siemens TRIO MRI system (Siemens AG, Erlangen, Germany) with a Siemens 32-channel head coil.",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n76",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "The first GLM (GLM1) included the following event types for each session",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n77",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "we analysed GLM1 parameter estimates from voxels of specific regions of interest (see Results) using mixed-effects linear regressions",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n78",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "we created another GLM (GLM2) with regressors designed to identify brain regions whose activation reflected the variables of the best-fitting computational model",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n79",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "We used the gPPI toolbox (McLaren et al., 2012) for SPM to run seed-to-voxel functional connectivity analyses.",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n80",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "we compared this brain signature to the neural responses obtained in our task",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n81",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "partners received painful stimuli when participants made errors during a difficult perception task",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n82",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "in separate conditions, the choice affected payoff either only for the participant or for all group members",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n83",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "A multivariate reanalysis of these two datasets revealed a neural signature for guilt",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n84",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "eLife 2026. DOI: 10.7554/eLife.105391",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n85",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "These errors evoked activations in the left aIns and dlPFC in the participants (Koban et al., 2013).",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n86",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "participants could decide to bear a proportion of their partner’s pain (Yu et al., 2014)",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n87",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "obtained a neural multivariate guilt-related brain signature (GRBS) (Yu et al., 2020)",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n88",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "reported involvement of medial prefrontal cortex, aIns and temporo-parietal junction (Edelson et al., 2018)",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n89",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "asking participants directly about which emotions they have felt during the different stages of this task",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n90",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Testing more participants would allow us to assess the impact of inter-individual variations in personality traits",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n91",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Using more trials in the experiment would allow separate modelling of risk preferences in gain and loss trials",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n92",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Varying partner identities (friends, stranger, and artificial agent) could reveal the impact of social discounting on guilt and responsibility.",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n93",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Functional connectivity analyses could also be performed for the data obtained in the feedback part of the paradigm.",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-n94",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "More experiments investigating specific computations in which these regions are involved",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r90",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "which suggests that this finding may not be very reliable",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r92",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "The fact that partner outcomes also influenced participants’ momentary happiness demonstrates",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r100",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "The stability of these estimated parameters was verified using a parameter recovery procedure",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r112",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Thus, activation in our insula ROIs increased in situations during which participants experienced guilt for low outcomes impacting their partner",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r113",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "is consistent with the mixed model analysis reported earlier",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r114",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "This finding suggests that this region of the left STS tracks a partner’s unexpected outcomes less when they do not follow from the participant’s decisions.",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r117",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "showed a significant similarity to a published guilt-related brain signature (Yu et al., 2020)",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r118",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "Results of a brief questionnaire indicate that this approach was successful",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r123",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "This confirms the importance of responsibility in determining the emotional consequences of risky social choices.",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r124",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "which we interpret as interpersonal guilt",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r125",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "we cannot exclude the possibility that they have instead or in addition felt empathy for their partner",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r126",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "may reflect the drive behind responsibility aversion reported by Edelson et al.’s 2018 study",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:a-r127",
      "@type": "Item",
      "format": "text/plain",
      "content": "replicating previous associations between this region and feelings of guilt",
      "has_container": "x:doc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:n0",
      "@type": [
        "x:_schema_Question",
        "Question"
      ],
      "title": "What neural mechanisms underlie guilt evoked by being responsible for a partner's uncertain outcomes in risky social decisions?",
      "content": "What neural mechanisms underlie guilt evoked by being responsible for a partner's uncertain outcomes in risky social decisions?\n\nThe paper targets a specific, understudied kind of guilt: that resulting from everyday choices that expose others to an uncertain outcome, in situations where the decision cannot be delegated.",
      "created": "2026-10-16T13:00:37.200Z",
      "modified": "2026-10-16T13:00:37.200Z",
      "creator": "x:agent",
      "description": "x:a-n0"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:n1",
      "@type": [
        "x:_schema_Question",
        "Question"
      ],
      "title": "Does responsibility for a partner's rewards (whether the participant or the partner chose) influence variations in the participant's momentary happiness?",
      "content": "Does responsibility for a partner's rewards (whether the participant or the partner chose) influence variations in the participant's momentary happiness?",
      "created": "2026-10-16T13:00:37.200Z",
      "modified": "2026-10-16T13:00:37.200Z",
      "creator": "x:agent",
      "description": "x:a-n1"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:n2",
      "@type": [
        "x:_schema_Question",
        "Question"
      ],
      "title": "Do risk preferences differ when participants choose only for themselves versus for themselves and a partner?",
      "content": "Do risk preferences differ when participants choose only for themselves versus for themselves and a partner?",
      "created": "2026-10-16T13:00:37.200Z",
      "modified": "2026-10-16T13:00:37.200Z",
      "creator": "x:agent",
      "description": "x:a-n2"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:n3",
      "@type": [
        "x:_schema_Claim",
        "Claim"
      ],
      "title": "Being responsible for a lottery choice that yields a low outcome for a partner decreases participant happiness more than witnessing the same outcome resulting from the partner's choice (a behavioural…",
      "content": "Being responsible for a lottery choice that yields a low outcome for a partner decreases participant happiness more than witnessing the same outcome resulting from the partner's choice (a behavioural 'guilt effect').\n\nThe effect is specific to low partner outcomes; it occurs whether the participant received the high or low lottery outcome, and is absent for positive partner outcomes. The authors interpret it as 'simple guilt' in the sense of psychological game theory.",
      "created": "2026-10-16T13:00:37.200Z",
      "modified": "2026-10-16T13:00:37.200Z",
      "creator": "x:agent",
      "description": "x:a-n3"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:n4",
      "@type": [
        "x:_schema_Claim",
        "Claim"
      ],
      "title": "The behavioural guilt effect is associated with increased BOLD signal in the left anterior insula.",
      "content": "The behavioural guilt effect is associated with increased BOLD signal in the left anterior insula.",
      "created": "2026-10-16T13:00:37.200Z",
      "modified": "2026-10-16T13:00:37.200Z",
      "creator": "x:agent",
      "description": "x:a-n4"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:n5",
      "@type": [
        "x:_schema_Claim",
        "Claim"
      ],
      "title": "Functional connectivity between the left anterior insula and the right inferior frontal gyrus during choice varies with choice type and social condition, suggesting the right IFG is sensitive to guil…",
      "content": "Functional connectivity between the left anterior insula and the right inferior frontal gyrus during choice varies with choice type and social condition, suggesting the right IFG is sensitive to guilt-related information during social choices.",
      "created": "2026-10-16T13:00:37.200Z",
      "modified": "2026-10-16T13:00:37.200Z",
      "creator": "x:agent",
      "description": "x:a-n5"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:n6",
      "@type": [
        "x:_schema_Claim",
        "Claim"
      ],
      "title": "Partner reward prediction errors, especially those resulting from the participant's own choices, contribute to explaining variations in participant momentary happiness beyond the participant's own re…",
      "content": "Partner reward prediction errors, especially those resulting from the participant's own choices, contribute to explaining variations in participant momentary happiness beyond the participant's own rewards and prediction errors.\n\nComputational models of happiness that include separate terms for partner reward prediction errors resulting from participant and partner choices (Responsibility and Responsibility Redux models) explain the data better than models without them.",
      "created": "2026-10-16T13:00:37.200Z",
      "modified": "2026-10-16T13:00:37.200Z",
      "creator": "x:agent",
      "description": "x:a-n6"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:n7",
      "@type": [
        "x:_schema_Claim",
        "Claim"
      ],
      "title": "A left superior temporal sulcus region tracks partner reward prediction errors that follow the participant's own choices more than those following partner choices, indicating a role in monitoring the…",
      "content": "A left superior temporal sulcus region tracks partner reward prediction errors that follow the participant's own choices more than those following partner choices, indicating a role in monitoring the consequences of one's risky decisions on others.",
      "created": "2026-10-16T13:00:37.200Z",
      "modified": "2026-10-16T13:00:37.200Z",
      "creator": "x:agent",
      "description": "x:a-n7"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:n8",
      "@type": [
        "x:_schema_Claim",
        "Claim"
      ],
      "title": "There is no strong evidence that risk preferences differ between deciding for oneself only and deciding for oneself and a partner.",
      "content": "There is no strong evidence that risk preferences differ between deciding for oneself only and deciding for oneself and a partner.\n\nA slight increase in risk aversion in the Social condition was seen with the CARA ρ parameter in Study 1 only, but ρ could be estimated reliably in a minority of participants; the more robust risk premium showed no difference in either study.",
      "created": "2026-10-16T13:00:37.200Z",
      "modified": "2026-10-16T13:00:37.200Z",
      "creator": "x:agent",
      "description": "x:a-n8"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:n9",
      "@type": [
        "x:_schema_Claim",
        "Claim"
      ],
      "title": "Participants experienced guilt when their choices led to low outcomes for their partner.",
      "content": "Participants experienced guilt when their choices led to low outcomes for their partner.",
      "created": "2026-10-16T13:00:37.200Z",
      "modified": "2026-10-16T13:00:37.200Z",
      "creator": "x:agent",
      "description": "x:a-n9"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:n10",
      "@type": [
        "x:_schema_Claim",
        "Claim"
      ],
      "title": "Being assigned the role of decider in a social setting lowers happiness independently of outcome, possibly reflecting the 'weight of responsibility'.",
      "content": "Being assigned the role of decider in a social setting lowers happiness independently of outcome, possibly reflecting the 'weight of responsibility'.",
      "created": "2026-10-16T13:00:37.200Z",
      "modified": "2026-10-16T13:00:37.200Z",
      "creator": "x:agent",
      "description": "x:a-n10"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:n11",
      "@type": [
        "x:_schema_Claim",
        "Claim"
      ],
      "title": "People associate a psychological cost with assuming responsibility for others' outcomes (responsibility aversion).",
      "content": "People associate a psychological cost with assuming responsibility for others' outcomes (responsibility aversion).",
      "created": "2026-10-16T13:00:37.200Z",
      "modified": "2026-10-16T13:00:37.200Z",
      "creator": "x:agent",
      "description": "x:a-n11"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:n12",
      "@type": [
        "x:_schema_Claim",
        "Claim"
      ],
      "title": "The anterior insula is associated with feelings of guilt evoked during social decisions.",
      "content": "The anterior insula is associated with feelings of guilt evoked during social decisions.",
      "created": "2026-10-16T13:00:37.200Z",
      "modified": "2026-10-16T13:00:37.200Z",
      "creator": "x:agent",
      "description": "x:a-n12"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:n13",
      "@type": [
        "x:_schema_Claim",
        "Claim"
      ],
      "title": "Deciding for both self and partner rather than for oneself alone increases activation in precuneus, left TPJ and medial prefrontal cortex, regions associated with social cognition.",
      "content": "Deciding for both self and partner rather than for oneself alone increases activation in precuneus, left TPJ and medial prefrontal cortex, regions associated with social cognition.",
      "created": "2026-10-16T13:00:37.200Z",
      "modified": "2026-10-16T13:00:37.200Z",
      "creator": "x:agent",
      "description": "x:a-n13"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:n14",
      "@type": [
        "x:_schema_Claim",
        "Claim"
      ],
      "title": "Ventral striatum is more engaged when choosing the risky than the safe option and its activation increases with expected rewards.",
      "content": "Ventral striatum is more engaged when choosing the risky than the safe option and its activation increases with expected rewards.",
      "created": "2026-10-16T13:00:37.200Z",
      "modified": "2026-10-16T13:00:37.200Z",
      "creator": "x:agent",
      "description": "x:a-n14"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:n15",
      "@type": [
        "x:_schema_Claim",
        "Claim"
      ],
      "title": "Participants were not emotionally detached from the consequences of their actions on their partner, even though the partner's decisions were in fact made by an algorithm.",
      "content": "Participants were not emotionally detached from the consequences of their actions on their partner, even though the partner's decisions were in fact made by an algorithm.",
      "created": "2026-10-16T13:00:37.200Z",
      "modified": "2026-10-16T13:00:37.200Z",
      "creator": "x:agent",
      "description": "x:a-n15"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:n16",
      "@type": [
        "x:_schema_Claim",
        "Claim"
      ],
      "title": "Participants' choices between safe and risky options tracked the difference between the lottery's expected value and the safe option's value.",
      "content": "Participants' choices between safe and risky options tracked the difference between the lottery's expected value and the safe option's value.",
      "created": "2026-10-16T13:00:37.200Z",
      "modified": "2026-10-16T13:00:37.200Z",
      "creator": "x:agent",
      "description": "x:a-n16"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:n17",
      "@type": [
        "x:_schema_Claim",
        "Claim"
      ],
      "title": "Participants' own reward prediction errors influence their happiness more than the partner's reward prediction errors.",
      "content": "Participants' own reward prediction errors influence their happiness more than the partner's reward prediction errors.",
      "created": "2026-10-16T13:00:37.200Z",
      "modified": "2026-10-16T13:00:37.200Z",
      "creator": "x:agent",
      "description": "x:a-n17"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:n18",
      "@type": [
        "x:_schema_Claim",
        "Claim"
      ],
      "title": "Information processed in the left STS is relayed to the inferior frontal gyrus during social decisions.",
      "content": "Information processed in the left STS is relayed to the inferior frontal gyrus during social decisions.",
      "created": "2026-10-16T13:00:37.200Z",
      "modified": "2026-10-16T13:00:37.200Z",
      "creator": "x:agent",
      "description": "x:a-n18"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:n19",
      "@type": [
        "x:_schema_Claim",
        "Claim"
      ],
      "title": "The icebreaker game created a positive, sympathetic social bond between participant and partner.",
      "content": "The icebreaker game created a positive, sympathetic social bond between participant and partner.",
      "created": "2026-10-16T13:00:37.200Z",
      "modified": "2026-10-16T13:00:37.200Z",
      "creator": "x:agent",
      "description": "x:a-n19"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:n20",
      "@type": [
        "x:_schema_Claim",
        "Claim"
      ],
      "title": "Participants may instead or in addition have felt empathy for the partner, a feeling of failure or bad luck, or another emotion rather than guilt, since emotions were not explicitly asked about.",
      "content": "Participants may instead or in addition have felt empathy for the partner, a feeling of failure or bad luck, or another emotion rather than guilt, since emotions were not explicitly asked about.",
      "created": "2026-10-16T13:00:37.200Z",
      "modified": "2026-10-16T13:00:37.200Z",
      "creator": "x:agent",
      "description": "x:a-n20"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:n21",
      "@type": [
        "x:_schema_Evidence",
        "Evidence"
      ],
      "title": "In Study 1, the probability of choosing the lottery increased with the expected-value difference between lottery and safe option (t(4796) = 9.26, p < 3.1e–20, β = 0.074, 95% CI [0.059 0.090]).",
      "content": "In Study 1, the probability of choosing the lottery increased with the expected-value difference between lottery and safe option (t(4796) = 9.26, p < 3.1e–20, β = 0.074, 95% CI [0.059 0.090]).",
      "created": "2026-10-16T13:00:37.200Z",
      "modified": "2026-10-16T13:00:37.200Z",
      "creator": "x:agent",
      "description": "x:a-n21",
      "sourceDocument": "https://doi.org/10.7554/eLife.105391"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:n22",
      "@type": [
        "x:_schema_Evidence",
        "Evidence"
      ],
      "title": "In Study 2, the probability of choosing the lottery increased with the expected-value difference between lottery and safe option (t(3829) = 10.62, p < 5.3e–26, β = 0.093, 95% CI [0.075 0.110]).",
      "content": "In Study 2, the probability of choosing the lottery increased with the expected-value difference between lottery and safe option (t(3829) = 10.62, p < 5.3e–26, β = 0.093, 95% CI [0.075 0.110]).",
      "created": "2026-10-16T13:00:37.200Z",
      "modified": "2026-10-16T13:00:37.200Z",
      "creator": "x:agent",
      "description": "x:a-n22",
      "sourceDocument": "https://doi.org/10.7554/eLife.105391"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:n23",
