    {
      "@id": "x:n60",
      "@type": [
        "x:_schema_Study",
        "Study"
      ],
      "title": "Study 1: behavioural experiment outside the MRI scanner in which 40 participants, paired with another participant, made risky versus safe monetary choices in Solo, Social and Partner conditions over …",
      "content": "Study 1: behavioural experiment outside the MRI scanner in which 40 participants, paired with another participant, made risky versus safe monetary choices in Solo, Social and Partner conditions over three sessions and rated momentary happiness every two trials.\n\nForty healthy participants (14 male, mean age 26.1, range 22–31). Partners were pairs of participants. Choices, risk preferences, and happiness were analysed with mixed-effects regressions, risk premium and CARA estimates, computational happiness models and LMMs.",
      "created": "2026-10-16T13:00:37.200Z",
      "modified": "2026-10-16T13:00:37.200Z",
      "creator": "x:agent",
      "description": "x:a-n60"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:n61",
      "@type": [
        "x:_schema_Study",
        "Study"
      ],
      "title": "Study 2: fMRI experiment in which 44 participants performed two sessions of the same risky-choice task with happiness ratings inside a 3T scanner, with experimenters MG or TW as partner.",
      "content": "Study 2: fMRI experiment in which 44 participants performed two sessions of the same risky-choice task with happiness ratings inside a 3T scanner, with experimenters MG or TW as partner.\n\n44 healthy participants (19 male, mean age 30.6, range 23–50); sample size from a G*Power estimate based on Study 1 (d = 0.56, alpha 0.05, power 0.95). ISIs varied from 3 to 11 s. fMRI data from four participants were excluded for excessive head motion. BOLD data analysed with GLM1 contrasts, ROI mixed models, model-based GLM2, PPI connectivity and comparison with a guilt-related brain signature.",
      "created": "2026-10-16T13:00:37.200Z",
      "modified": "2026-10-16T13:00:37.200Z",
      "creator": "x:agent",
      "description": "x:a-n61"
    },
    {
      "@id": "x:n62",
